  "date": "12-10",
  "text": "With the catastrophe out of the bag, the USSR scrambled to contain the damage. They sealed off an “Exclusion Zone” around the plant — at first 10 kilometers, later expanding to 30 kilometers — and evacuated tens of thousands of people from Pripyat and the surrounding villages. Firefighters, miners, and a half-million Soviet soldiers were mobilized. It took them two weeks to extinguish the fire at the core of the reactor; within seven months, a containment “sarcophagus” had been installed over the meltdown site.",
